<title>ITALY: Italy's Palermo sees March CPI +0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Palermo sees March CPI +0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO, Italy 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Palermo said its March consumer price index stood at +0.2 percent month on month and +1.8 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In February, Palermo's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 1.8 percent respectively. The general index and the housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of a court ruling that reversed electricity tariff reductions.</p>
<p>Palermo is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI weighs 6.80 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to February 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.2    (0.1R)   1.8    (1.8R)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.1   (-0.2)    2.9    (3.1)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.4   (-0.1)    2.2    (2.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -0.1    (0.7R)   1.0    (1.1R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.2   (-0.5)    0.0    (0.1)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2    (0.2)    3.1    (3.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3    (0.0)    1.6    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.2    (0.6)    1.2    (1.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.8    (0.4)    4.3    (3.4)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1    (0.4)    1.5    (1.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.7    (0.1)   -0.2   (-0.9)</p>
<p>R - revised</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
